---
description: Global rules for the ManualKitBundle repository (nowo-tech/manual-kit-bundle)
alwaysApply: true
---

This repository is a reusable Symfony bundle: an in-app product manual rendered from the host's `docs/manual`
Markdown (`src/`, namespace `Nowo\ManualKitBundle\`, config root `nowo_manual_kit`).

Prefer:
- minimal, local changes, starting with the files already open or explicitly mentioned
- the smallest viable patch first
- preserving backward compatibility of config keys, route names (`nowo_manual_*`), Twig functions and template paths
- running the repository gates through the Makefile (`make qa`, `make release-check`) — they run inside Docker

Do not scan the whole repository unless explicitly required.
Do not read `vendor/`, `node_modules/`, `coverage/`, `coverage-ts/`, `var/`, `demo/symfony8/vendor/`, lock files or
`src/Resources/public/js/manual-lightbox.js` (generated) unless the task needs them.
